Hi

After some months of playing a lawful human valkirye, I finally ascended,
it feels good.

The beginning of the game was very uncertain, as it took me more than 3600
turns to find the downstairs to dlvl2, but I've been lucky with finding food
and praying when I was fainting, and I was already at xp:5 when I went
down. A general store there allowed me to price'id a few scrolls, a wand and
some potions. I also found a  vault that I would loot later. I almost died to
rothes on dlvl3 due to AC 10. I went back up to dlvl1 to heal and found another
vault there. At dlvl4 I realised that AC 10 was because I was not wearing the
small shield for some reason. Found the second general store, and the entrance
to the Mines. Before going to the Mines I wanted to dip for Excalibur, and
found a fountain dlvl5 where I successfully dipped my long sword. Also found a
cross-aligned altar. 

I went to the Mines, and hurried to Minetown as I had no light and all the
levels were dark until there. I bought a katana in the general shop with
twoweaponing in mind, and buc'ed it at the co-aligned altar :-)
I reduced my AC to 1 with some pieces of armor found in the levels before.
Izchak had a brass lantern, a magic lamp that I bought and some candles that I
would buy later. Having now everlasting light I visited carefully the levels up
Minetown, and found a pick-axe. Back to the dungeons I was at xp:9 and started
twoweaponing Excalibur and a katana, being expert in long swords.

On my way to Sokoban I found a elven mithril coat that turned out to be cursed.
I thought I would try dip it in fountains until it would be uncursed (I had
never tried this before). I dipped the cursed armor in the Oracle's fountains
and got it uncursed. I realized when I wore it that it had a negative
enchantment. Still I gained one AC point by wearing it. I had a blessed scroll
of either remove curse or enchant armor, so I read it and got "Your elven
mithril-coat glows silver for a while", great :-)
I got the BoH in sokoban and collected some rings and elven daggers that I
buc'ed at the altar dlvl5. Trying the rings I identified gain constitution,
adornment and invisibility. I dropped some of them along some other items
because I was burdened.

A fourth general store was on dlvl10 where I bought some scrolls of identify,
enchant weapon and enchant armor. I also bought an ornamental cope. Out of the
shop an ant soldier reduced my hp to 5(88), so I prayed and Tyr was
well-pleased, I felt much better. I stepped on a teleport trap on dlvl11 and
was carried to dlvl3. It was time to use my pick-axe and loot the two vaults I
found earlier. I stopped at the altar on the way down, my ornamental cope was
cursed, I dropped it. I had converted the altar before, and got some luck boost
by sacrificing the random monsters popping up. I was given a wish by sitting on
a throne dlvl11, and got blessed greased +2 sdsm.

The portal to the quest was dlvl15, but i was only xp:12 so I kept on
exploring down. I had some wands of create monster so I headed down to the
altar dlvl5 for sacfesting, got Mojo and Demonbane that I would drop later. The
wand gave me my first unihorn, and I felt approprietly lawful by offering the
unicorn corpse. I went to finish the mines, and polymorphed into a silver
dragon in Mine's End. There a Vampire Lord drained me two levels, as a Dragon I
was not wielding Excalibur, lesson learned. The teleport trap under the
luckstone in the Catacombs sent me to dlvl4, I didn't have to go through the
Mines again. I spent some more time at the altar.

I polymorphed into a silver dragon for the second time on dlvl19 where I also
found an armor shop with nothing interesting in it. I went down one more time
to the altar to have some stuff buc'ed. I left the altar with hp 108(108) and
AC: -7. At the Oracle I diluted a bunch of potions to make holy water, and then
rustproofed and enchanted my katana. Also blessed some id scrolls and had my
full inventory identified: I had a scroll of genocide and a scroll of charging
among other things. After blessing them I genocided the 'L'. I earned some more
money in a leprechaun hall dlvl20. Dlvl23 was a temple, I bought some
protection. Dancing with a nurse increased my max hp a bit. I found another
scroll of genocide and killed a captain from who I got a silver saber.

Once again, a teleport trap sent me up to dlvl6, so I spent more time at the
altar. On the way up I was still not ready for the Quest. Back to dlvl23 I met
a incubus, I will omit the details but after the "meeting" I was at XP:14. Time
for the Quest. Nothing special really, I decided to left the giants there for
when I would have a way to eat them all. I killed Surtur easily enough, and
kept on descending. Dlvl25 was Medusa's lair, I digged down, and stepped on a
tel trap to find myself back to dlvl2 in the general store. I bought some boots
a ring and an amulet. The boots turned out to be blessed boots of walking
water, allowing me to dilute easily potions. With the newly made holy water I
blessed and enchanted a stack of 9 elven daggers.

The wand in the Castle dlvl29 provided me a blessed fixed +2 CoMR, a magic
marker and a blessed fixed +2 pair of speed boots. I wished a bit later for a
blessed ring of levitation to fly over the pits of the castle. Then I went back
to dlvl23 at the temple of Loki to BUC stuff. I had an amulet of magical
breathing, and a wererat identified for me the "oLS. Went to the quest levels to
eat all those giants. Back to the temple I had str:18/90 and offered my last
gold to gain one more AC point and clairvoyance, "I bestow upon thee a
blessing." After blessing and enchanting my silver saber to +7 I was ready for
Gehennom. I had AC -31 at this point and 27 potions of holy water.

The twoweaponing Exca/silver saber was really efficient in VotD. Before going
deeper I read a blessed scroll of genocide and "Wiped out all hobbits.  Wiped
out all dwarves.  Wiped out all bugbears.  Wiped out all dwarf lords. Wiped out
all dwarf kings.  Wiped out all mind flayers.  Wiped out all master mind
flayers." The RNG gave me three wraiths corpses in a row, that was quite
exceptional. I reached XP:22. One of the chests had just another scroll of
genocide, hey, nice. I polypiled for fun 4 scrolls of create monster and got 4
scrolls of enchant weapon that i transformed further in scrolls of identify. I
already had +6 Exca, +7 silver saber and 9 +6 elven daggers in the quiver.

Finally i was entering Gehennom. I explored the mazes alternating twoweaponing
and wielding my pick-axe to make straight ways between the stairs in case I
would survive the trip down and have to come up. I had some troubles to find
Vlad's tower entrance, so i went down. In Orcus Town I was lucky to
get a fresh cockatrice corpse and petrify Orcus, and after crushing his statue
with my pick-axe I read a scroll of identify to know the charges of the wand of
death, it was (0:3). On dlvl40 I realized that I forgot to buy the candles in
Minetown. I asked on #nethack channel if i should go back or wish for them, and
someone suggested to use cursed scrolls of teleport. I made 4 of them with some
unholy water and was back to dlvl6 in one turn (and 2 scrolls). I bought 8
candles and found a magic marker in a room I didn't visit yet. I wrote a cursed
scroll of genocide and was sent some wraiths, but none of them left a corpse.
So I tried again out of the Mines and reached XP:24. 

Back in Hell, I found the stairs to Vlad and took the stuff from him. Nothing
special. I could now replace magical breathing with life saving. At the bottom
of Gehennom I marked the vibrating square with a lizard corpse and 
went up to the Wizard. I killed him with a rubber chicken, took the book after
destroying the statue and headed down. I entered the Sanctum on turn 65493,
just after wishing for a ring of conflict. I found the secret door quickly and
meleed the High Priestess, who died short after. I picked up the Amulet and
tried to teleport with a scroll, but were told that I felt disoriented. Okay, I
will have to go up by the stairs.

The ascension run went flawlessly, the mysterious force hit some times but was
not a big deal. I zapped death at Rodney when he appeared, and I didn't see his
double. Crossing the Planes of Earth was easy, it took me 60 turns to reach the
magic portal. The Air was not more difficult, I found my way away from the
hordes of E. The portal on the Fire Planes was straight up at top right corner
of the map. I was there quickly. Idem for the Planes of Water, it went in a
breeze. I had reached the Astral Planes for the first time, what a mess up
there. I put on my ring of conflict, located Death, Famine and Pestilence and
went to the Altar on the left, which was neutral. Hmm, I so went to the next on
the right, and killed Pestilence on the way. The second Altar was to Loki, no
luck. Death came close to me, I hit him two times and he was no more. One hit
killed Famine, and I entered the temple on the right, and there, well offered
the Amulet and were granted the gift...

